X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260909T160000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research + Cite It Right with NoodleTools
DESCRIPTION:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliog
 raphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features
 \, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs. This worksho
 p will use the MLA citation style\, which is typically used in the Englis
 h\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and Religion disciplines.  If you are
  using APA\, take this workshop! We will share how to choose this option 
 in NoodleTools too.  You will learn how to sign up for an account with No
 odleTools. We will provide examples to show how to create citations\, cre
 ate a bibliography and check for errors.  Along the way\, you will receiv
 e quick tips on how to find credible research in the library and on the w
 eb.  Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option to submit your instr
 uctor and course name when you register if you would like us to notify yo
 ur instructor that you have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, 
 you can work with your instructor on an alternative way to provide eviden
 ce of your attendance.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA
  citations and bibliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and 
 paper-writing features\, including the capability to create papers via Go
 ogleDocs. This workshop will use the MLA citation style\, which is typica
 lly used in the English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and Religion di
 sciplines.</p><p>  If you are using APA\, take this workshop! We will sha
 re how to choose this option in NoodleTools too.</p><p>  You will learn h
 ow to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples t
 o show how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for erro
 rs.</p><p>  Along the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find cr
 edible research in the library and on the web.</p><p>  Extra Credit: As s
 tudents\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course name w
 hen you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that you 
 have attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your 
 instructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.<
 /p>
