SUMMARY:Opening Reception - Tom Chown: 46 Years Behind the Lens
DESCRIPTION:Chown began his career at SRJC at age 24\, working in the cam
 pus photography lab. Over the next 46 years\, he became a familiar presen
 ce throughout the college community\, documenting the people\, programs a
 nd milestones that shaped generations of students and employees.  The exh
 ibition will trace Chown's evolution as a photographer\, from working wit
 h film and developing photographs in the darkroom to embracing digital ph
 otography. It also offers a visual history of SRJC\, preserving moments f
 rom nearly five decades of college life.  A selection of photographs in t
 he exhibit will be available for bidding\, with 100% of the proceeds bene
 fiting the SRJC Foundation's Jeanne Chown Memorial Nursing Scholarship. E
 stablished in 1998 in honor of Chown's mother\, the scholarship supports 
 students pursuing careers in nursing.Location: Robert F. Agrella Art Gall
 ery\, Doyle Library 1st floor - Santa Rosa CampusFor more information\, v
 isit SRJC's Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery website. (https://art-gallery.s
 antarosa.edu/exhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Chown began his career at SRJC at age 2
 4\, working in the campus photography lab. Over the next 46 years\, he be
 came a familiar presence throughout the college community\, documenting t
 he people\, programs and milestones that shaped generations of students a
 nd employees.</p><p>  The exhibition will trace Chown's evolution as a ph
 otographer\, from working with film and developing photographs in the dar
 kroom to embracing digital photography. It also offers a visual history o
 f SRJC\, preserving moments from nearly five decades of college life.</p>
 <p>  A selection of photographs in the exhibit will be available for bidd
 ing\, with 100% of the proceeds benefiting the SRJC Foundation's Jeanne C
 hown Memorial Nursing Scholarship. Established in 1998 in honor of Chown'
 s mother\, the scholarship supports students pursuing careers in nursing.
 </p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery\, Doyle L
 ibrary 1st floor - Santa Rosa Campus</p><p><a href="https://art-gallery.s
 antarosa.edu/exhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work" target="_blank" rel="noo
 pener">For more information\, visit SRJC's Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery 
