BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
LOCATION:Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery - Santa Rosa Campus
SUMMARY:Tom Chown: 46 Years Behind the Lens
DESCRIPTION:Santa Rosa Junior College will celebrate the 46-year career o
 f longtime staff photographer Tom Chown with a photography exhibition fea
 turing images from his decades at the college\, from the days of film and
  darkrooms to the digital era.  Chown began his career at SRJC at age 24\
 , working in the campus photography lab. Over the next 46 years\, he beca
 me a familiar presence throughout the college community\, documenting the
  people\, programs and milestones that shaped generations of students and
  employees.  The exhibition will trace Chown's evolution as a photographe
 r\, from working with film and developing photographs in the darkroom to 
 embracing digital photography. It also offers a visual history of SRJC\, 
 preserving moments from nearly five decades of college life.  The exhibit
 ion is free and open to the public.Location: Robert F. Agrella Art Galler
 y\, Doyle Library 1st floor - Santa Rosa CampusFor more information\, vis
 it SRJC's Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery website. (https://art-gallery.san
 tarosa.edu/exhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Santa Rosa Junior College will celebrat
 e the 46-year career of longtime staff photographer Tom Chown with a phot
 ography exhibition featuring images from his decades at the college\, fro
 m the days of film and darkrooms to the digital era.</p><p>  Chown began 
 his career at SRJC at age 24\, working in the campus photography lab. Ove
 r the next 46 years\, he became a familiar presence throughout the colleg
 e community\, documenting the people\, programs and milestones that shape
 d generations of students and employees.</p><p>  The exhibition will trac
 e Chown's evolution as a photographer\, from working with film and develo
 ping photographs in the darkroom to embracing digital photography. It als
 o offers a visual history of SRJC\, preserving moments from nearly five d
 ecades of college life.</p><p>  The exhibition is free and open to the pu
 blic.</p><p><strong>Location:</strong> Robert F. Agrella Art Gallery\, Do
 yle Library 1st floor - Santa Rosa Campus</p><p><a href="https://art-gall
 ery.santarosa.edu/exhibition/tom-chown-i-surevy-work" target="_blank" rel
 ="noopener">For more information\, visit SRJC's Robert F. Agrella Art Gal
 lery website.</a></p>
