X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260921T180000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research + Cite It Right with NoodleTools
DESCRIPTION:NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliog
 raphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features
 \, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.  This Noodle
 Tools workshop will use the MLA citation style\, which is typically used 
 in the English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and Religion disciplines
 . If you are using APA\, take this workshop! We will share how to choose 
 this option in NoodleTools too.  You will learn how to sign up for an acc
 ount with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show how to create cit
 ations\, create a bibliography and check for errors. Along the way\, you 
 will receive quick tips on how to find credible research in the library a
 nd on the web.  Check with your instructor to confirm the citation style 
 appropriate for your research assignment.  Extra Credit: As students\, yo
 u have the option to submit your instructor and course name when you regi
 ster if you would like us to notify your instructor that you have attende
 d the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor o
 n an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA
  citations and bibliographies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and 
 paper-writing features\, including the capability to create papers via Go
 ogleDocs.</p><p>  This NoodleTools workshop will use the MLA citation sty
 le\, which is typically used in the English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosop
 hy\, and Religion disciplines. If you are using APA\, take this workshop!
  We will share how to choose this option in NoodleTools too.</p><p>  You 
 will learn how to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provid
 e examples to show how to create citations\, create a bibliography and ch
 eck for errors. Along the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to fin
 d credible research in the library and on the web.</p><p>  Check with you
 r instructor to confirm the citation style appropriate for your research 
 assignment.</p><p><br />  Extra Credit: As students\, you have the option
  to submit your instructor and course name when you register if you would
  like us to notify your instructor that you have attended the workshop fo
 r extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternative 
 way to provide evidence of your attendance.</p>
