BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Santa Rosa Junior College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T120000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Reg Rodriguez - Human Agency & Machine Inquiry
DESCRIPTION:As generative AI becomes embedded across disciplines\, higher
  education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle between opposing camps\
 , but of intentional design.  Generative systems offer novel capabilities
  for research\, creation\, and learning\, yet their ultimate value depend
 s entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them.Reg Rodriguez serves as subj
 ect matter expert evaluating the quality and accuracy of AI-generated leg
 al content.Learn more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website. (ht
 tps://cs.santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  As generative AI becomes embedded acros
 s disciplines\, higher education faces a pivotal moment—not of battle b
 etween opposing camps\, but of intentional design.</p><p>  Generative sys
 tems offer novel capabilities for research\, creation\, and learning\, ye
 t their ultimate value depends entirely on how thoughtfully we guide them
 .</p><p><strong>Reg Rodriguez</strong> serves as subject matter expert ev
 aluating the quality and accuracy of AI-generated legal content.</p><p><a
  href="https://cs.santarosa.edu/ai-talks-2026" target="_blank" rel="noope
 ner">Learn more on the SRJC Computer Studies' AI Talks website.</a></p>
