SUMMARY:Standing in Her Power: Portraits Beyond the Colonial Frame
DESCRIPTION:In early May 2026\, we put out a call for nominations\, askin
 g for Native American women to represent their Nations\, their stories\, 
 and their strength through a powerful portrait exhibition celebrating ide
 ntity\, cultural legacy\, and the resilience of Native women. Every singl
 e entry showed us how beautiful and unique and strong Native American wom
 en are.  Two days of photo sessions were held in the Museum in August wit
 h photographer Alexa Treviňo of LexMex Art.This Exhibit is funded by a g
 rant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultur
 al Enrichment Endowment.For more information\, visit the SRJC Multicultur
 al Museum website. (https://museum.santarosa.edu/event/standing-her-power
